<title>NETHERLANDS: DELTA LLOYD BANK REITERATES IHC CALAND BUY.</title>
<headline>DELTA LLOYD BANK REITERATES IHC CALAND BUY.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of Jan 31 research.</p>
<p>    Company-------Sector----------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>    IHC Caland    Capital Goods   103.00  Delta Lloyd Bank</p>
<p>COMMENT: &quot;IHC's order portfolio is well filled until far into</p>
<p>1998. We expect earnings growth of well over 15 percent for both</p>
<p>1997 and 1998. We think that its price is justifiable as IHC has</p>
<p>proven itself to be somewhat of a growth stock in the last few</p>
<p>years. Prospects remain good for this technically advanced</p>
<p>company and we reiterate our buy,&quot; writes analyst Peter Wortel.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS	  P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995 (actual)	3.16	 34.0    1.60</p>
<p>    1996		   3.70	 29.0    1.75</p>
<p>    1997		   4.20	 25.5    2.05</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
